# The console bundle in web/dist is generated output: CI rebuilds it and fails
# when the bytes differ from what is committed. Marking it binary stops Git
# converting line endings on checkout/commit (core.autocrlf is commonly on for
# Windows checkouts), so a bundle built here is byte-identical to one built on
# the Linux CI runner.
web/dist/** -text -diff

# The bundle check compares a Linux CI build against a build made with a
# Windows checkout. Svelte compiles template-literal line endings straight
# into the output JS, so a CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true) produces
# different bytes - and different asset hashes - from the same sources.
# Force LF for the web sources so both platforms compile identical output.
web/index.html text eol=lf
web/src/** text eol=lf

# Shell scripts are executed by sh and embedded into the binary with
# include_str!, so a CRLF checkout would both break the update helper's
# json_escape test (which slices the function out on a "\n}\n" boundary) and
# ship scripts the updater cannot run. Keep them LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
